#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:11
msgid ""
"Custom React PropType validators that we use at Airbnb. Use of [airbnb-"
"js-shims](https://npmjs.com/package/airbnb-js-shims) or the equivalent is"
" recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:13
msgid "`and`: ensure that all provided propType validators pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:14
msgid "`foo: and([number, nonNegativeInteger])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:15
msgid ""
"`between`: provide an object with an `gt` or `gte` number, and an `lt` or"
" `lte` number (only one item allowed from each pairs; one or both pairs "
"may be provided), and the resulting propType validator will ensure the "
"prop value is a number within the given range. Alternatively, you can "
"provide a function that takes the `props` object and returns a number for"
" each of the `gt`/`gte`/`lt`/`lte` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`foo: between({ gte: 0, lte: 5 })`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:17
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`foo: between({ gt: 0, lt: 5 })`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:18
msgid ""
"`booleanSome`: provide a list of props, and all must be booleans, and at "
"least one of them must be `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:19
msgid "`foo: booleanSome('small', 'medium', 'large')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:20
msgid ""
"`childrenHavePropXorChildren`: ensure that either all children have the "
"indicated prop, all children have children, or all children have neither."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:21
msgid "`foo: childrenHavePropXorChildren('bar')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:22
msgid ""
"`childrenOf`: restrict the children prop to only allow children that pass"
" the given propType validator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:23
msgid "`children: childrenOf(number.isRequired)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:24
msgid ""
"`childrenOfType`: restrict the children prop to only allow children of "
"the given element types - takes a Component, an HTML tag name, or `\"*\"`"
" to match everything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:25
msgid "`children: childrenOfType('span')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:26
msgid "`children: childrenOfType(Component)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:27
msgid ""
"`childrenSequenceOf`: restrict the children prop to be a sequenceOf the "
"given \"specifiers\" (see `sequenceOf`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:28
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`children: childrenSequenceOf({validator: string, min: 0, max: 5})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:29
msgid ""
"`componentWithName`: restrict the prop to only allow a component with a "
"certain name/displayName. Accepts a string, or a regular expression. Also"
" accepts an `options` object with an optional `stripHOCs` array of string"
" HOC names to strip off before validating; an HOC name must not contain "
"parentheses and must be in camelCase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:30
msgid "`foo: componentWithName('Component')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:31
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`foo: componentWithName('Component', { stripHOCs: ['withDirection', "
"'withStyles'] })`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:32
msgid ""
"`disallowedIf`: restrict the prop from being provided if the given other "
"prop name matches the given other prop type. The other prop type "
"validator only applies if the other prop name is not a null value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:33
msgid "`foo: disallowedIf(string, 'bar', bool)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:34
msgid ""
"`elementType`: require that the prop be a specific type of React element "
"- takes a Component, an HTML tag name, or `\"*\"` to match everything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:35
msgid "`foo: elementType('span')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:36
msgid "`foo: elementType(Component)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:37
msgid ""
"`empty`: a value that React renders to nothing: `undefined`, `null`, "
"`false`, the empty string, or an array of those things."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:38
msgid "`foo: empty()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:39
msgid ""
"`explicitNull`: only allow `null` or `undefined`/omission - and only "
"`null` when required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:40
msgid "`foo: explicitNull()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:41
msgid ""
"`forbidExtraProps`: pass your entire `propTypes` object into this "
"function, and any nonspecified prop will error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:42
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`Component.propTypes = forbidExtraProps({foo: number.isRequired})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:43
msgid "`integer`: require the prop be an integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:44
msgid "`foo: integer()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:45
msgid ""
"`keysOf`: pass in a proptype, and require all the keys of a prop to have "
"that type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:46
msgid "`foo: keysOf(number)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:47
msgid ""
"`mutuallyExclusiveProps`: provide a propType, and a list of props, and "
"only one prop out of the list will be permitted, validated by the given "
"propType."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:48
msgid "`foo: mutuallyExclusiveProps(bool, 'bar', 'sna')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:49
msgid ""
"`mutuallyExclusiveTrueProps`: provide a list of props, and all must be "
"booleans, and only one is allowed to be true."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:50
msgid "`foo: mutuallyExclusiveTrueProps('bar', 'sna')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:51
msgid "`nChildren`: require a specific amount of children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:52
msgid "`children: nChildren(3)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:53
msgid "`children: nChildren(3, childrenOfType('span'))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:54
msgid ""
"`nonNegativeInteger`: require that the prop be a number, that is 0, or a "
"finite positive integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:55
msgid "`foo: nonNegativeInteger()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:56
msgid ""
"`nonNegativeNumber`: require that the prop be a number, that is 0, or a "
"finite positive number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:57
msgid "`foo: nonNegativeNumber()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:58
msgid ""
"`numericString`: require the prop be a string that is conceptually "
"numeric."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:59
msgid "`foo: numericString()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:60
msgid ""
"`object`: same as `PropTypes.object`, but can be called outside of "
"React's propType flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:61
msgid ""
"`or`: recursively allows only the provided propTypes, or arrays of those "
"propTypes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:62
msgid "`foo: or([bool.isRequired, explicitNull()])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:63
msgid ""
"`predicate`: provide a predicate function, and an optional message, and "
"will fail when the predicate returns false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:64
msgid "`foo: predicate((x) => x % 2 === 0, 'must be an even integer')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:65
msgid ""
"`range`: provide a min, and a max, and the prop must be an integer in the"
" range `[min, max)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:66
msgid "`foo: range(-1, 2)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:67
msgid ""
"`ref`: require the prop to be a React ref. These can be either the object"
" returned from `React.createRef()` or \"callback\" refs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:68
msgid "`foo: ref()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:69
msgid ""
"`requiredBy`: pass in a prop name and propType, and require that the prop"
" is defined and is not its default value if the passed in prop name is "
"truthy. if the default value is not provided, defaults to checking "
"against `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:70
msgid "`foo: requiredBy('bar', bool)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:71
msgid ""
"`restrictedProp`: this prop is not permitted to be anything but `null` or"
" `undefined`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:72
msgid "`foo: restrictedProp()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:73
msgid "`foo: restrictedProp(new TypeError('Custom Error'))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:74
msgid ""
"`sequenceOf`: takes 1 or more \"specifiers\": an object with a "
"\"validator\" function (a propType validator), a \"min\" "
"nonNegativeInteger, and a \"max\" nonNegativeInteger. If both \"min\" and"
" \"max\" may be omitted, they default to 1; if only \"max\" is omitted, "
"it defaults to Infinity; if only \"min\" is omitted, it defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:75
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`foo: sequenceOf({validator: string, min: 0, max: 5})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:76
msgid ""
"`shape`: takes a shape, and allows it to be enforced on any non-"
"null/undefined value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:77
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`foo: shape({ length: oneOf([2]) })`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:78
msgid ""
"`stringEndsWith`: takes a non-empty string, and returns a validator that "
"ensures the prop value is a string that ends with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:79
msgid "`foo: stringEndsWith('.png')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:80
msgid ""
"`stringStartsWith`: takes a non-empty string, and returns a validator "
"that ensures the prop value is a string that starts with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:81
msgid "`foo: stringStartsWith('prefix-')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:82
msgid ""
"`uniqueArray`: this prop must be an array, and all values must be unique "
"(determined by `Object.is`). Like `PropTypes.array`, but with uniqueness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:83
msgid "`foo: uniqueArray()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:84
msgid ""
"`uniqueArrayOf`: `uniqueArray`, with a type validator applied. Like "
"`PropTypes.arrayOf`, but with uniqueness. Can also take an optional "
"mapper function that allows for a non-standard unique calculation "
"(otherwise, `Object.is` is used by default). The function is applied to "
"each element in the array, and the resulting values are compared using "
"the standard unique calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:85
msgid "`foo: uniqueArrayOf(number)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:86
msgid "`foo: uniqueArrayOf(element => element ** 2)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:87
msgid "`foo: uniqueArrayOf(element => element ** 2, 'test')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:88
msgid "`foo: uniqueArrayOf(array, element => element[0] ** 2, 'test')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:89
msgid ""
"`valuesOf`: a non-object requiring `PropTypes.objectOf`. Takes a propType"
" validator, and applies it to every own value on the propValue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:90
msgid "`foo: valuesOf(number)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:91
msgid ""
"`withShape`: takes a PropType and a shape, and allows it to be enforced "
"on any non-null/undefined value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:92
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`foo: withShape(array, { length: oneOf([2]) })`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:94
msgid "Production"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/airbnb-prop-types_README.md:95
msgid ""
"Since `PropTypes` are typically not included in production builds of "
"React, this library’s functionality serves no useful purpose. As such, "
"when the `NODE_ENV` environment variable is `\"production\"`, instead of "
"exporting the implementations of all these prop types, we export mock "
"functions - in other words, something that ensures that no exceptions are"
" thrown, but does no validation. When environment variables are inlined "
"(via a browserify transform or webpack plugin), then tools like webpack "
"or uglify are able to determine that only the mocks will be imported - "
"and can avoid including the entire implementations in the final bundle "
"that is sent to the browser. This allows for a much smaller ultimate file"
" size, and faster in-browser performance, without sacrificing the "
"benefits of `PropTypes` themselves."
msgstr ""

